{"url": "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/admission-onboarding/prepare/gre", "final_url": "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/admission-onboarding/prepare/gre", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-12", "text": "Graduate School\nOff screen link: Skip to content\nOff screen link: Skip to search\nMain Menu\nDean's Initiatives, Awards & Events\nDean's Initiatives, Awards & Events Submenu\nAdmission & Onboarding\n, (current section)\nAdmission & Onboarding Submenu\nAcademics\nAcademics Submenu\nFinancial Support\nFinancial Support Submenu\nProfessional Development\nProfessional Development Submenu\nDiversity\nStudent Experience\nStudent Experience Submenu\nAlumni\nStudent Support: At a Glance\nAbout\nAbout SubMenu\nNews\nEvents\nPolicies\nStay in Touch\nAdmin Portal\nAPPLY\nSearch\nHome\nAdmission and Onboarding\nPrepare Your Application\nSection Menu\nExplore\nPrepare\n, (current section)\nApplication Deadlines\nApplication Fee\nAcademic Statement of Purpose\nPersonal Statement\nResume / Curriculum Vitae\nLetters of Recommendation\nTranscripts\nFall Semester Grades\nGRE\n, (current page)\nEnglish Proficiency\nWriting Sample\nStatement of Financial Resources\nApply\nReview Admission Decision\nOnboard & Arrive\nNondegree Programs\nGRE\nGuidelines for Applicants\nDegree programs may require Graduate School applicants, including master\u2019s students and those not applying directly out of college, to submit valid GRE scores to be considered for admission.\nThe Graduate School does not have a minimum score requirement; each department or program may set its own. The Graduate School does not have average GRE scores, however, departments or programs may.\nSend test scores no later than three weeks before the degree program application deadline to ensure receipt of the official score report. Test scores received after the deadline will still be matched to your application; however, faculty may have already begun their review of your application without your test scores. No offers of admission will be made if required scores are not in the application. You do not need to wait on test scores to submit your application. If your application is on file when scores are received, we will match them to your application within seven business days.\nGRE\nApplicants may be required to submit valid General Test scores from Educational Testing Service (ETS). Other than the GMAT exception noted below, no other test scores (including the LSAT) may be submitted in their place. For more information about the GRE\n, contact ETS\n.\nGRE Requirements: General & Subject Tests\nGRE Table: Requirements for Fall 2027 Admission\nGRE Planning and Deadlines\nGRE Home Testing\nValid GRE Scores & Reporting\nGMAT\nApplicants applying to the Department of Finance\nmay submit valid GMAT scores in place of GRE scores. No other department or program accepts GMAT. GMAT is offered on a monthly basis. For more information, visit GMAT\n.\nGMAT Online\nValid GMAT Scores & Reporting\nScore Validity and Review\nOnly valid, unexpired test scores will be considered.\nBeginning with Fall 2026 admission, test scores will only be considered if they remain valid as of the date the application opens (September 15). Scores that expire before the application opening date\u2014even if submitted earlier\u2014will not be accepted.\nFrequently Asked Questions\nWhat is Princeton\u2019s institution and department code for the GRE?\nCan I submit expired, partial, or self-reported scores?\nDo I need to resubmit scores sent previously?\nHow do I know if you received my test scores?\nI see a test date on my checklist, but it is not the date I took the test. What should I do?\nWhat do I do if there is a discrepancy in my name between my test and application?\nI had my scores sent and submitted my application but still do not see the test dates on my application checklist. What should I do?\nBack to\nTop\nFOOTER\nPrinceton University Graduate School\nClio Hall, Princeton, NJ, 08544\nContact: gs@princeton.edu\nAccessibility Guides: Clio Hall and University Buildings\nX\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nDiversity & Non-Discrimination\nAccessibility Help\n\u00a9 2026 The Trustees of Princeton University\nm", "links": [["Off screen link: Skip to content", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/admission-onboarding/prepare/gre#main-content"], ["Off screen link: Skip to search", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/admission-onboarding/prepare/gre#edit-search-keys"], ["", "http://www.princeton.edu"], ["", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/"], ["Dean's Initiatives, Awards & Events", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events"], ["About the Dean", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/about-dean"], ["Dean Rodney Priestley", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/about/our-staff/rodney-d-priestley"], ["Dean's Dispatches", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/about-dean/deans-dispatches"], ["Dean\u2019s Leadership Council", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/about-dean/dean%E2%80%99s-leadership-council"], ["Dean\u2019s Initiatives", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/dean%E2%80%99s-initiatives"], ["Strategic Planning", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/dean%E2%80%99s-initiatives/strategic-planning"], ["Elevating Mentorship", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/dean%E2%80%99s-initiatives/elevating-mentorship"], ["What Is Mentoring at Princeton?", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/dean%E2%80%99s-initiatives/elevating-mentorship/what-mentoring-princeton"], ["Elevating Mentorship Initiative", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/dean%E2%80%99s-initiatives/elevating-mentorship/elevating-mentorship"], ["Community of Mentors", "https://gradschool.princeton.edu/deans-initiatives-awards-events/dean%E2%80%99s-initi